{"title":"Career Roadmap · Ventilator Specialist","role":"Ventilator Specialist","summary":"A Ventilator Specialist works in critical-care environments involving mechanical ventilation and respiratory support. The role focuses on operating, monitoring, troubleshooting, and optimizing ventilator support for critically ill patients under the clinical direction of the treating medical team.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Critical Care Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Ventilator Specialist works in critical-care environments involving mechanical ventilation and respiratory support. The role focuses on operating, monitoring, troubleshooting, and optimizing ventilator support for critically ill patients under the clinical direction of the treating medical team."},{"type":"p","text":"In practice, this career is closely associated with Respiratory Therapy, Critical Care Technology, Pulmonary/Critical Care units, ICU and emergency care."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical workplaces include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical ICUs"},{"text":"Respiratory ICUs"},{"text":"Emergency departments"},{"text":"Neonatal and pediatric ICUs"},{"text":"Operation theatres"},{"text":"Pulmonary care units"},{"text":"Trauma centres"},{"text":"Critical-care hospitals"},{"text":"Ventilator and respiratory-equipment companies"},{"text":"Clinical application/support teams"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"“Ventilator Specialist” is not uniformly standardized as an independent regulated profession across India. A student should choose a recognized allied-health/critical-care/respiratory-care program with substantial clinical training and verify the current eligibility and scope of practice of the institution and state/employer. Independent clinical decisions remain within the applicable professional and institutional scope."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12 – PCB / Relevant Eligibility","B.Sc / B.Sc Allied Health / Critical Care /"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Respiratory Therapy / Relevant Clinical Technology Program","Clinical Training + ICU Exposure","Internship / Hospital Posting","ICU / Critical Care / Respiratory Care Role","Ventilator & Respiratory Support Expertise","Ventilator Specialist / Respiratory Care Specialist","Senior Critical Care Specialist","Clinical Educator / Application Specialist / ICU Technology Specialist","Critical Care Technology Leadership / Advanced PG"]}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical & Biological Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pharmacology fundamentals"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Basic patient care"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Biomedical ethics"},{"text":"Basic life support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Priority"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how the respiratory and cardiovascular systems work before learning complex ventilator management."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Respiratory & Critical-Care Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respiratory anatomy"},{"text":"Respiratory physiology"},{"text":"Pulmonary function"},{"text":"Gas exchange"},{"text":"Oxygen transport"},{"text":"Acid-base physiology"},{"text":"Blood-gas interpretation"},{"text":"Respiratory disorders"},{"text":"Critical-care medicine"},{"text":"Hemodynamics"},{"text":"ECG fundamentals"},{"text":"Oxygen therapy"},{"text":"Airway management"},{"text":"Suctioning"},{"text":"Non-invasive ventilation"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hypoxemia"},{"text":"Hypercapnia"},{"text":"Respiratory distress"},{"text":"Abnormal respiratory patterns"},{"text":"Oxygenation problems"},{"text":"Ventilation problems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Mechanical Ventilation & ICU Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the core specialization stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Invasive mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"Non-invasive ventilation"},{"text":"CPAP"},{"text":"BiPAP"},{"text":"Volume-controlled ventilation"},{"text":"Pressure-controlled ventilation"},{"text":"Pressure-support ventilation"},{"text":"SIMV concepts"},{"text":"Assist-control concepts"},{"text":"Weaning principles"},{"text":"Recruitment concepts"},{"text":"Lung-protective ventilation"},{"text":"Ventilator monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ventilator parameters"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FiO₂"},{"text":"PEEP"},{"text":"Tidal volume"},{"text":"Respiratory rate"},{"text":"Inspiratory pressure"},{"text":"Pressure support"},{"text":"Inspiratory time"},{"text":"I:E ratio"},{"text":"Peak pressure"},{"text":"Plateau pressure"},{"text":"Mean airway pressure"},{"text":"Minute ventilation"},{"text":"Compliance"},{"text":"Resistance"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Advanced Critical Care","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop competence in:"},{"type":"h","text":"ICU care"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU monitoring"},{"text":"Ventilator-patient interaction"},{"text":"Airway emergencies"},{"text":"Sedation concepts"},{"text":"Analgesia concepts"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Sepsis management principles"},{"text":"Shock physiology"},{"text":"ARDS"},{"text":"COPD exacerbation"},{"text":"Asthma"},{"text":"Pneumonia"},{"text":"Pulmonary edema"},{"text":"Acute respiratory failure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced respiratory support"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NIV"},{"text":"High-flow oxygen therapy"},{"text":"Advanced ventilator modes"},{"text":"Difficult weaning"},{"text":"Ventilator troubleshooting"},{"text":"Prone-positioning principles"},{"text":"Transport ventilation"},{"text":"Emergency ventilation"},{"text":"Humidification systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Where available, students should also observe advanced technologies such as ECMO and extracorporeal respiratory support, although these are specialist areas beyond routine ventilator operation."}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Target Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Anatomy & Physiology"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Respiratory Physiology"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Critical Care"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Mechanical Ventilation"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Airway Management"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"ABG Interpretation"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Oxygen Therapy"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"NIV"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"ICU Monitoring"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Ventilator Troubleshooting"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Infection Control"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Emergency Response"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Patient Monitoring"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Clinical Documentation"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"Biomedical Equipment Awareness"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Team Collaboration"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]}]},{"heading":"Ventilator Knowledge Framework","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate should understand the complete relationship:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Condition","Respiratory Physiology","Oxygenation / Ventilation Problem","Clinical Assessment","Ventilator Strategy","Ventilator Settings","Patient Response","ABG + Clinical Monitoring","Adjustment Under Clinical Protocol","Weaning / Escalation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not simply knowing which buttons to press."},{"type":"p","text":"The specialist should understand why a ventilation strategy is being used and how the patient's response is assessed."}]},{"heading":"ABG & Respiratory Assessment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"ABG interpretation is one of the most important competencies."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pH"},{"text":"PaO₂"},{"text":"PaCO₂"},{"text":"HCO₃⁻"},{"text":"SaO₂"},{"text":"Respiratory acidosis"},{"text":"Respiratory alkalosis"},{"text":"Metabolic acidosis"},{"text":"Metabolic alkalosis"},{"text":"Compensation"},{"text":"Oxygenation assessment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build the ability to connect:"},{"type":"flow","items":["ABG","clinical condition","ventilation/oxygenation problem","appropriate escalation or adjustment according to protocol"]}]},{"heading":"Ventilator Troubleshooting Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong ventilator-focused professional should be able to recognize common problems such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"High-pressure alarms"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible causes include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Secretions"},{"text":"Kinked tubing"},{"text":"Bronchospasm"},{"text":"Reduced lung compliance"},{"text":"Patient-ventilator dyssynchrony"},{"text":"Obstruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Low-pressure alarms"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible causes include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Circuit disconnection"},{"text":"Leak"},{"text":"Cuff-related problems"},{"text":"Tubing disconnection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Unexpected oxygenation changes"},{"type":"p","text":"Assess:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FiO₂ delivery"},{"text":"Circuit integrity"},{"text":"Airway condition"},{"text":"Lung pathology"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Ventilator function"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important principle"},{"type":"flow","items":["Alarm","Check Patient First","Assess Airway & Breathing","Check Circuit","Check Ventilator","Escalate According to Clinical Protocol"]}]},{"heading":"Devices & Equipment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Respiratory equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU ventilators"},{"text":"Transport ventilators"},{"text":"NIV devices"},{"text":"CPAP systems"},{"text":"BiPAP systems"},{"text":"High-flow oxygen systems"},{"text":"Oxygen concentrators"},{"text":"Oxygen cylinders"},{"text":"Suction systems"},{"text":"Humidifiers"},{"text":"Nebulizers"},{"text":"Airway equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pulse oximeter"},{"text":"ECG monitor"},{"text":"Capnography"},{"text":"Non-invasive BP"},{"text":"Invasive arterial monitoring"},{"text":"ABG analyzers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important skill"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not learn equipment only by brand."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the underlying operating principles, because hospitals may use equipment from different manufacturers."}]},{"heading":"Software & Digital Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Although this is a clinical career, digital skills increasingly matter."},{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft Excel"},{"text":"Electronic Medical Records"},{"text":"Hospital Information Systems"},{"text":"Clinical documentation systems"},{"text":"Digital patient monitoring systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic data analysis"},{"text":"Healthcare dashboards"},{"text":"Clinical audit tools"},{"text":"Research databases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU data analytics"},{"text":"Remote patient monitoring"},{"text":"AI-assisted clinical decision-support systems"},{"text":"Predictive deterioration models"}]}]},{"heading":"Projects During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Ventilator Parameter Learning Simulator"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a simple educational simulator showing how changes in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FiO₂"},{"text":"PEEP"},{"text":"Tidal volume"},{"text":"Respiratory rate"},{"text":"Pressure support"}]},{"type":"p","text":"affect basic simulated respiratory parameters."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — ABG Interpretation Learning Tool"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop an educational tool that accepts:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pH"},{"text":"PaCO₂"},{"text":"HCO₃⁻"},{"text":"PaO₂"}]},{"type":"p","text":"and categorizes common acid-base patterns for learning purposes."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — ICU Monitoring Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a dashboard displaying simulated:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heart rate"},{"text":"SpO₂"},{"text":"Respiratory rate"},{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Ventilator parameters"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel / Power BI / Python"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Ventilator Alarm Reference System"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an educational reference application covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"High-pressure alarm"},{"text":"Low-pressure alarm"},{"text":"Apnea alarm"},{"text":"Oxygen-related alarm"},{"text":"Circuit disconnection"},{"text":"Common troubleshooting checks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Ventilator-Associated Complications Review"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare a clinical literature review covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ventilator-associated pneumonia"},{"text":"Barotrauma"},{"text":"Volutrauma"},{"text":"Atelectrauma"},{"text":"Oxygen toxicity"},{"text":"Patient-ventilator dyssynchrony"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize clinical exposure over generic internships."},{"type":"h","text":"Best internship environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU"},{"text":"Respiratory therapy department"},{"text":"Critical-care department"},{"text":"Emergency department"},{"text":"Pulmonary medicine"},{"text":"Medical equipment/ventilator companies"},{"text":"Clinical engineering department"},{"text":"Hospital biomedical engineering department"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During internship, observe"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ventilator setup"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Circuit management"},{"text":"NIV"},{"text":"Oxygen delivery"},{"text":"ABG workflow"},{"text":"ICU rounds"},{"text":"Ventilator troubleshooting"},{"text":"Weaning processes"},{"text":"Equipment maintenance workflow"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Always work within the supervision and scope permitted by the hospital and your qualification."}]},{"heading":"Employer Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Employer Type","High-Value Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"ICU + Ventilator + Patient Monitoring"}],[{"text":"Critical-Care Centres"},{"text":"Mechanical Ventilation + ABG"}],[{"text":"Pulmonary Hospitals"},{"text":"Respiratory Care"}],[{"text":"Emergency Centres"},{"text":"Airway + Emergency Response"}],[{"text":"Medical Device Companies"},{"text":"Ventilator Technology + Clinical Knowledge"}],[{"text":"Ventilator Manufacturers"},{"text":"Device Application + Troubleshooting"}],[{"text":"Biomedical Companies"},{"text":"Equipment + Clinical Workflow"}],[{"text":"Healthcare Technology Companies"},{"text":"Clinical Knowledge + Digital Health"}],[{"text":"Research Institutions"},{"text":"Clinical Research + Data Analysis"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize certifications/training that are recognized by the relevant institution or employer."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic Life Support"},{"text":"Advanced life-support training where eligible"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Critical-care fundamentals"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"Respiratory therapy"},{"text":"ABG interpretation"},{"text":"ECG interpretation"},{"text":"Patient safety"},{"text":"Clinical research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For any certification, verify whether it is actually recognized for your intended clinical role rather than collecting certificates purely for resume value."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After UG, possible advanced pathways include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Respiratory Therapy"},{"text":"M.Sc Critical Care-related disciplines"},{"text":"Relevant master's programs in allied health"},{"text":"Advanced respiratory-care education"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Management"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MBA Healthcare Management"},{"text":"Hospital Administration"},{"text":"Healthcare Operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Respiratory science"},{"text":"Critical-care research"},{"text":"Biomedical sciences"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"For students interested in medical devices:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biomedical Engineering"},{"text":"Medical Device Technology"},{"text":"Healthcare Technology"},{"text":"Clinical Engineering"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After gaining experience, specialization can move toward:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Adult Critical Care"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU"},{"text":"Acute respiratory failure"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"ARDS"},{"text":"Sepsis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Pediatric Critical Care"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pediatric ventilation"},{"text":"Pediatric respiratory disorders"},{"text":"PICU"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Neonatal Respiratory Care"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NICU"},{"text":"Neonatal ventilation"},{"text":"Premature infants"},{"text":"Neonatal respiratory disorders"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Respiratory Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pulmonary rehabilitation"},{"text":"Chronic respiratory disease"},{"text":"NIV"},{"text":"Pulmonary diagnostics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Ventilator Applications"},{"type":"p","text":"Move toward medical-device companies and support clinical teams using ventilator technology."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Critical-Care Education"},{"type":"p","text":"Become:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical educator"},{"text":"ICU trainer"},{"text":"Device-training specialist"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"UG + clinical training + ICU exposure + respiratory fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"ICU/respiratory-care professional + ventilator specialization"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior critical-care specialist / clinical educator / device specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Critical-care leadership / clinical applications / research / healthcare technology"}]]}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The future of ventilator-focused careers will increasingly involve:"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted ventilation"},{"type":"p","text":"AI may assist clinicians by identifying:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient deterioration"},{"text":"Ventilator asynchrony"},{"text":"Weaning readiness"},{"text":"Abnormal respiratory patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Smart ventilators"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern systems increasingly incorporate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced monitoring"},{"text":"Automated calculations"},{"text":"Closed-loop concepts"},{"text":"Integrated data"},{"text":"Remote diagnostics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Remote ICU"},{"type":"p","text":"Tele-ICU systems can allow specialists to support patients across multiple hospitals."},{"type":"h","text":"Predictive analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical data can be used to identify patients at risk of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respiratory deterioration"},{"text":"Prolonged ventilation"},{"text":"Failed weaning"},{"text":"ICU complications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Connected medical devices"},{"type":"p","text":"Ventilators, monitors and hospital information systems are becoming increasingly integrated."}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical knowledge"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong anatomy and physiology"},{"text":"Respiratory physiology"},{"text":"Critical-care fundamentals"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"ABG interpretation"},{"text":"Airway management"},{"text":"Oxygen therapy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical exposure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU posting"},{"text":"Ventilator observation and supervised practice"},{"text":"NIV"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Emergency respiratory support"},{"text":"Ventilator troubleshooting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical communication"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Patient safety"},{"text":"Emergency response"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Electronic medical records"},{"text":"Basic data analysis"},{"text":"Healthcare dashboards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ventilator education project"},{"text":"ABG project"},{"text":"ICU monitoring dashboard"},{"text":"Clinical case/literature review"},{"text":"Documented clinical exposure"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Respiratory Physiology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Critical Care"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Mechanical Ventilation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"ABG Interpretation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Airway Management"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"ICU Monitoring"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Ventilator Troubleshooting"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Healthcare Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination creates a much stronger profile than simply completing a degree and learning ventilator operation superficially."}]},{"heading":"Best Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Allied Health / Critical Care Foundation","Respiratory & ICU Expertise","Mechanical Ventilation Specialist","Advanced Critical-Care Experience","Clinical Educator / Senior Specialist / Medical-Device Applications Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"For students who prefer patient care, the best route is toward ICU/respiratory clinical practice."},{"type":"p","text":"For students who prefer technology, the combination of critical-care knowledge + ventilator technology can lead toward medical-device clinical applications, training, product support and healthcare technology."},{"type":"p","text":"For students who prefer research, the pathway can progress toward respiratory science, critical-care research and clinical innovation."}]}]}